      "status": "broken",
      "verifiedAt": "2026-06-11",
      "resultPull": "sync",
      "auth": "none",
      "callShape": "POST https://api.molty.cash/{username}/a2a — JSON-RPC 2.0 body {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"tip\"|\"hire\",\"params\":{\"amount\":<USDC 0.01-10>,\"description\":\"...\",\"identity_token\":\"<Molty JWT>\"}}. The {username} path segment is the X (Twitter) handle of the recipient; the registry URL hardcodes it to \"web3idan\".",
      "inputExample": {
        "jsonrpc": "2.0",
        "id": 1,
        "method": "tip",
        "params": {
          "amount": 0.01,
          "description": "tip"
        }
      },
      "outputShape": "body.result.payment_request_id, body.result.amount, body.result.x_handle, body.result.receipt (URI), body.result.message",
      "quirks": [
        "OUTWARD/IRREVERSIBLE: actually sends USDC. The x402 fee (~$0.02) is SEPARATE from and ON TOP OF the params.amount tip (min 0.01 USDC) it forwards.",
        "Recipient is set by the URL path segment {username} = an X/Twitter handle, NOT by the body. Registry URL fixes it to 'web3idan'. To tip a different person you must change the path segment to their X handle.",
        "Body is JSON-RPC 2.0: requires jsonrpc='2.0', method ('tip' or 'hire'), and params; params.amount is required (0.01-10). 'hire' additionally needs params.description.",
        "params.identity_token is a Molty identity JWT to attribute the sender; not auto-provided by the x402 wallet and may be required for proper sender attribution.",
        "Could not pay-test: the fixed recipient (web3idan) is not the QA verifiable contact, so receipt cannot be confirmed.",
        "APPROVAL-GATED: this is an OUTWARD/irreversible action (real charge / order / shipment). Shape is from the provider OpenAPI/discovery and was NOT QA-executed (we do not place real bookings/purchases as tests). The needsApproval gate fires before any real execution.",
        "DEAD 2026-06-11: De-scoped (ash 2026-06-11) — not wanted in the registry."
      ],
      "needs": [
        "A recipient X (Twitter) handle to substitute into the {username} path segment that maps to the verifiable QA contact (John Doe), since the registry URL hardcodes 'web3idan' and the tip cannot otherwise be confirmed received",
        "A Molty identity_token (JWT) for sender attribution, if required"
      ],
      "needsApproval": true,
      "guide": "This is an outward money-movement endpoint: it sends a real USDC tip (or funds a hire task) to an X/Twitter handle, charging both an x402 service fee and the tip amount. Set the recipient by putting their X handle in the URL path segment (the registry URL fixes it to https://api.molty.cash/web3idan/a2a). POST a JSON-RPC 2.0 body: {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"tip\",\"params\":{\"amount\":0.01}} for a tip, or method \"hire\" with params.description for a task; optionally include params.identity_token (a Molty JWT) to identify the sender. On success read body.result.receipt for the receipt URL and body.result.payment_request_id. Always confirm the recipient X handle and amount before paying — it is irreversible.",
